# CI/CD

## Two pipelines — one logic

| | GitHub Actions | GitLab CI |
|---|---|---|
| Config | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | `.gitlab-ci.yml` |
| Trigger | push/PR to main, develop | push/MR to main, develop |
| Runner | GitHub-hosted | GitLab runners (tagged) |

All logic lives in npm scripts — CI files only orchestrate.

## Stages

```
check → e2e → build (Electron)
```

### check (on every push/PR)

| Step | npm command |
|------|-----------|
| TypeScript | `npm run typecheck` |
| ESLint | `npm run lint` |
| Prettier | `npm run format:check` |
| Unit tests | `npm run test` |
| Build web | `npm run build --workspace=web` |
| Security audit | `npm audit --audit-level=high` |

### e2e (after check)

| Step | npm command |
|------|-----------|
| Install browsers | `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium` |
| Run tests | `npm run e2e -- --project=chromium` |

### build (main only)

| Platform | npm command | Runner tag |
|----------|-----------|-----------|
| Linux | `npm run package:electron:linux` | `linux` |
| Windows | `npm run package:electron:win` | `windows` |
| macOS | `npm run package:electron:mac` | `macos` |

## Synchronization rule

When modifying the pipeline:
1. Update BOTH files (`.github/workflows/ci.yml` + `.gitlab-ci.yml`)
2. Both must call the same npm scripts
3. Do not add logic to CI files — only to npm scripts

## Env vars in CI

| Variable | GitHub | GitLab |
|----------|--------|--------|
| Commit SHA | `${{ github.sha }}` | `$CI_COMMIT_SHA` |
| Branch | `${{ github.ref_name }}` | `$CI_COMMIT_BRANCH` |
| Is main | `github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'` | `$CI_COMMIT_BRANCH == "main"` |
| Artifacts | `actions/upload-artifact@v4` | `artifacts: paths:` |
